{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence","id":75951,"title":"[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-20T16:49:07-08:00","id":75951,"title":"[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence","content":"I'd thought it'd be interesting to start a thread about what would push various gods to pray for the Exigence in order to obtain an Exalted champion. Based on the spoilers we've had so far, I'm assuming Exigents are Exalted when gods are faced with a massive threat to their purview that they're too weak to resist. So, starting with...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sunipa, Goddess of Eastern War</span><br /> <br /> Sunipa's purview includes honourable rules of engagement, military discipline, elite units, Dragon-Blooded officers and duelist-champions. Potential threats to her domain include:<br /> - An invasion from the Realm, which would likely shift the focus of Eastern warfare away from elite units and back to full legions. In addition, the prevalence of Dragon-Blooded officers and champions of the Realm might cause Sunipa's patronage of the Dragon-Blooded to slip back to Tachi-Kun, the God of Central Warfare and technical patron of the Realm's warfare.<br /> - Barbarian hordes commanded by Lunars have no care for the proper rules of engagement. A massive beastfolk invasion would force the states of the River Province to turn away from Sunipa's military and religious doctrine in order to survive.<br /> - Solar warlords rise and begin conquering neighbouring lands in the name of their personal glory, which goes against Sunipa's military ethics and causes her power to wane as other warlords follow suit.<br /> - Mask of Winter's undead legions are sustained by mass slaughter. Not only does he ignore the honourable rules of engagement, his conquest of the East will likely render Sunipa obsolete eventually if he is not opposed.<br /> - The return of the Solars means a rise in Solar champion-duelist who also fall under Sunipa's purview. This threatens to undermine her patronage of the Dragon-Blooded, as well as the support she received from the Bronze Faction.<br /> - A fallen tyrant Exalts as a Getimian and begins to encourage wars of disproportionate retribution throughout the East. The bloodshed and resentment escalate at a rapid pace, making peace between the nations impossible. The Celestial Bureaucracy's influence over eastern warfare erodes, creating new opportunities for Rakan Thulio and his allies to expand their war against Heaven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T08:16:37-08:00","id":76283,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\">Nara-O, God of Secrets </span><br /> <br /> Nara-O's purview includes secrets that are only known to one person. Possible threats to his purview include:<br /> - An Infernal plans to enslave all of humanity within a world-spanning hive mind, which would eliminate the possibility of secrets. This would destroy both Nara-O and the Forbidding Manse of Ivy. <br /> - Itzcalimon has used his powers of blackmail to obtain a Black Market Exaltation from a god who had petitioned the Unconquered Sun for the Exigence. The Chosen of Blackmail is stealing records from Nara-O's office and using them as leverage against gods, mortals and Exalted alike. Nara-O's power wanes the more of his secrets are used for blackmail, and Itzcalimon threatens to replace Nara-O's place in the Forbidding Manse of Ivy as his own influence grows. <br /> - The true names of the Deathknights are lost to Heaven, and Nara-O cannot stand this insult. He has tasked his Exalted champion with recovering the names and history of all the Abyssal Exalted so that his records may be complete. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T08:06:56-08:00","id":77653,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ruvia, God of Roads</span><br /> <br /> Ruvia is primarily the god of roads, but he also serves as the head of the Golden Barque of the Heavens, as well as the captain of the Barque itself. Potential threats to his purview include:<br /> - A Lunar and her Infernal mate have engineered a plan to destroy the Realm. The Lunar's beastfolk legion will go forth, destroying all the roads used by the Realm's Legions, while the Infernal will summon Jacint into Creation to build new roads. This will allow the two Exalted to control all of the Realm's transportation. It is also likely to destroy several hundred road gods, Ruvia himself, and possibly the Golden Barque of the Heavens as a whole.<br /> - The return of the Solar artisans has allowed Vanileth to regain some measure of his power, and he grows more influential with each passing day. If left unchecked, artificial flight will one day return as the primary mode of transportation, and Ruvia may very well lose his position as the captain of the Barque. He needs an Exalted champion to defend and develop major roads, or else to subvert Vanileth's portfolio into his own. <br /> - A Deathknight familiar with the forbidden roads of the Labyrinth has offered to guide major caravans through the Underworld so that they might reach their destination faster. The Guild has gladly accepted her offer and now, many road gods are demanding horrific human sacrifices so that their roads might be turned into shadowlands and become part of the Deathknight's circuit. If this is allowed to continue, Creation's major roads will fall into the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T04:38:28-08:00","id":84502,"title":"","content":"Nice going with this.<br /> I've not put much thought into why specific canonical gods need the Exigence but some more general thoughts about why it'll improve their role in the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T06:19:08-08:00","id":84527,"title":"","content":"The Exigence is interesting. Solars and Lunars kinda-sorta Exalt when they need it, but Exigents seem to Exalt when a god needs it. They're more about the world's problems than people's problems with the world.<br /> <br /> Which is actually why the Solars and Lunars were created in the first place, and raises interesting questions about the ethics of their current role as Exalted champions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T06:40:15-08:00","id":84539,"title":"","content":"This may have been answered, or we may simply not know, but:<br /> <br /> Solar and Lunar, et al, Exaltations are loosed and not under the direct management of the sponsor, which is why they seem to affect individuals who need them more than individuals the god needs at the time. <br /> <br /> Certainly the first recipient of an Exigence seems to be selectable. What if that person dies? Does the Exigence continue as other Exaltations, finding suitable candidates? Does it vanish or return to UCS?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T06:45:10-08:00","id":84544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=84539#post84539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly the first recipient of an Exigence seems to be selectable. What if that person dies? Does the Exigence continue as other Exaltations, finding suitable candidates? Does it vanish or return to UCS?</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually the Exaltation perishes with the host like with Dragon-Blooded and Alchemicals, however there are exceptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T07:05:54-08:00","id":84557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=84544#post84544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Usually the Exaltation perishes with the host like with Dragon-Blooded and Alchemicals, however there are exceptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that something we've been told? I was under the impression it was up to the God (player/ST) designing the new Exaltation if they wanted it to be a permanent thing or not...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T07:13:01-08:00","id":84561,"title":"","content":"I think the managing god will decide if they choose from a pool of eligible candidates or if it will pass father to first born son, or mother to first born daughter. Or how ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T07:17:37-08:00","id":84562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=84527#post84527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Exigence is interesting. Solars and Lunars kinda-sorta Exalt when they need it, but Exigents seem to Exalt when a god needs it. They're more about the world's problems than people's problems with the world.<br /> <br /> Which is actually why the Solars and Lunars were created in the first place, and raises interesting questions about the ethics of their current role as Exalted champions.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I don't quite get about Exigence as presented is why it has to do with the Sun and the Solars. As I understand it, the Exigence largely disappears when the Solars do, and reactivates when they come back. But the problem with that is that the Solars vanishing is EXACTLY when the gods need it!<br /> <br /> The Spirit Bureaucracies in the First Age were set up so that, if there was a problem, the local god followed a chain of command and submitted a request for Exalted, the lords of the earth, to come round and check it out. If no Solars were available, some Celestial would be dispatched, and failing that, a bunch of Dragon-Blooded. When this system is functioning, which it mostly did, there'd be no need for Exigents.<br /> <br /> However, once the Usurpation hit, not only are there no Solars or Lunars to appeal to, but the Sidereals are seen as traitors (and too busy to help in any case) and the Dragon-Blooded are no longer trusted. This is the perfect time for Exigence to be a big deal! It really seems to me that the Shogunate is the period where Exigents should really shine!<br /> <br /> But sadly, that's not a playable era. But it would still be cool to pepper the backstory of Creation with the notion that these guys had been very active and influential back then! Not every new Exalt need be new to the setting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T07:48:02-08:00","id":84587,"title":"","content":"I agree there Hand of Omega. You make a good point about how it doesn't need to be that new. If other gods discovered how to make an Exalted essence Then the shogunate is when these would have made their debute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T09:21:46-08:00","id":84645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=84557#post84557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Is that something we've been told?</div> </div> </div> </div>That Creation isn't overrun with the Exaltations of long-dead gods? Yes. I remember it coming up in response to people screaming &quot;RUINED FOREVER!&quot; at the notion of more exalt types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T09:23:42-08:00","id":84647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=84587#post84587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree there Hand of Omega. You make a good point about how it doesn't need to be that new. If other gods discovered how to make an Exalted essence Then the shogunate is when these would have made their debute.</div> </div> </div> </div>They did - the Liminals first popped up in the Shogunate.<br /> <br /> It seems to me that the absence of the Exigence during the Shogunate is precisely the point, showing the problem with having the Exigence being dependent on the UCS to hand out - and what it means that it is once more being handed out.<br /> <br /> Something else of relevance is that the capacity to create Exalted singlehandedly appears to be limited to god-figures of a certain standing - the Celestial Incarnae, the Five Elemental Dragons, the Yozis, Autochthon, etc. That is, it does not appear to be something any god can do ex nihilo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T09:41:12-08:00","id":84658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=84645#post84645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That Creation isn't overrun with the Exaltations of long-dead gods? Yes. I remember it coming up in response to people screaming &quot;RUINED FOREVER!&quot; at the notion of more exalt types.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, thanks!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ~~It seems to me that the absence of the Exigence during the Shogunate is precisely the point, showing the problem with having the Exigence being dependent on the UCS to hand out - and what it means that it is once more being handed out.<br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>Do we know anything about the relationship between the Sun, the Solars and the Exigence? Does it becoming active again mean that TUS is actively interested in Creation again? That's a pretty big change from previous editions...Or is it just dependent on the Solar exaltations being in the world for some reason?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T09:50:37-08:00","id":84661,"title":"","content":"Based on the Strawmaiden Janest fiction, gods need to pray to the Unconquered Sun to be able to use the Exigence. I assume the decay of the Exigence has to do with the Unconquered Sun turning away from Creation. Now that the Solars are back, the Unconquered Sun is paying attention again and the Exigence is more accessible. It could also be that the Exigence was part of the collateral damage of the Usurpation, or was tied to the Jade Prison somehow. <br /> <br /> Or maybe it'll never be explained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T11:41:00-08:00","id":84747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=84557#post84557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that something we've been told? I was under the impression it was up to the God (player/ST) designing the new Exaltation if they wanted it to be a permanent thing or not...</div> </div> </div> </div>Holden mentioned that the overwhelming majority of Exigents are one-shot deals, in response to a post where I was speculating about different methods of transmission. I'll try to track it down, but I think it may have been on the old forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T12:28:37-08:00","id":84777,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://nishkriya.com/Threads/Details/2226\" target=\"_blank\">Found it</a>! Unfortunately, the post he's responding to<i> is</i> on the old forum, and he didn't quote it, but I guess it's clear enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T17:18:57-08:00","id":84940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=84661#post84661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on the Strawmaiden Janest fiction, gods need to pray to the Unconquered Sun to be able to use the Exigence. I assume the decay of the Exigence has to do with the Unconquered Sun turning away from Creation. Now that the Solars are back, the Unconquered Sun is paying attention again and the Exigence is more accessible. It could also be that the Exigence was part of the collateral damage of the Usurpation, or was tied to the Jade Prison somehow.<br /> <br /> Or maybe it'll never be explained.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might be something I alter in my version of creation, The demands upon anything less than a celestial incarni will be too great for anything more than 1 or 2 sparks but definitely something they would want. What with the thousand god revolt against the Rose Empress and the Phoenix Empress it seems to make sense they would want this power for themselves, and not want to have to wait for UCS to rubber stamp their application.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T17:29:51-08:00","id":84946,"title":"","content":"That's what Black Market Exaltations are for! It's not like prohibition ever stopped people from getting their hands on delicious illegal swag.<br /> <br /> Wait.<br /> <br /> Divine Al Capone selling Black Market Exaltations. <br /> <br /> Chejop Kejack is Sean Connery. <br /> <br /> <i>Yeeeeeesssssssssss.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T18:16:47-08:00","id":84974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=84940#post84940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be something I alter in my version of creation, The demands upon anything less than a celestial incarni will be too great for anything more than 1 or 2 sparks but definitely something they would want. What with the thousand god revolt against the Rose Empress and the Phoenix Empress it seems to make sense they would want this power for themselves, and not want to have to wait for UCS to rubber stamp their application.</div> </div> </div> </div>No clue about the Rose Empress and Phoenix Empress in your Creation (wouldn't mind details, since they sound neat), but it's also worth noting that not every god who would want to have an Exalt of its own will be willing to pay the price of using the Exigence, even were access unlimited. Ten Sheaves died in the act of Exalting Janest, and while not all gods perish in using the Exigence, all dev remarks point to it always taking some non-trivial toll. Aside from that, as Tiresias points out, if gods without the Sun's sanction do want it, that's what the so-called Black Market Exaltations are for: a deity is granted access to the Exigence, and for whatever reason doesn't use it, that access passing over time to a god who has not sought the Sun's approval making use of it.<br /> <br /> Beginning by pointing out it's only my opinion, I might also caution against a flat &quot;1-2 sparks.&quot; Partly because there's a broad spectrum of power for gods that I feel it neglects, but mostly because it seems to carry the implicit assumption that all Exigents function basically like Celestial Exalted. The devs really do mean it when they say each Exigent is its own new type of Exalt. I mean, players and STs making Exigents will likely consider the general Solar/Lunar* Exalt mold as the default, but I feel it cuts off too many possibilities to treat it as the only one.<br /> <br /> * i.e. The Exaltation just goes to someone meeting the god's standards after the old bearer croaks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T15:29:14-07:00","id":87773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=84974#post84974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No clue about the Rose Empress and Phoenix Empress in your Creation (wouldn't mind details, since they sound neat), Beginning by pointing out it's only my opinion, I might also caution against a flat &quot;1-2 sparks.&quot; Partly because there's a broad spectrum of power for gods that I feel it neglects, but mostly because it seems to carry the implicit assumption that all Exigents function basically like Celestial Exalted. The devs really do mean it when they say each Exigent is its own new type of Exalt. I mean, players and STs making Exigents will likely consider the general Solar/Lunar* Exalt mold as the default, but I feel it cuts off too many possibilities to treat it as the only one. * i.e. The Exaltation just goes to someone meeting the god's standards after the old bearer croaks.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's not a flat 1 or 2 just that most terrestrial gods will only want to invest in that many. In my creation it's 10 years after the &quot;return of the Scarlet Empress. Due to circumstances she made Tepet Evaja her successor in a hurried decision. She became the Rose Empress. The Phoenix Empress is Menmon's name and she has taken the north, and northern East from Rose. Her fledgling empire and it's war against the Rose sparked the terrestrial God's rebellion. Which started with the bloody salt battle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T14:29:39-07:00","id":103639,"title":"","content":"Write something...<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=84946#post84946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what Black Market Exaltations are for! It's not like prohibition ever stopped people from getting their hands on delicious illegal swag.<br /> <br /> Wait.<br /> <br /> Divine Al Capone selling Black Market Exaltations.<br /> <br /> Chejop Kejack is Sean Connery.<br /> <br /> <i>Yeeeeeesssssssssss.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;He pulls a daiklave, you pull an Essence Cannon. He sends one of yours to the hospice, you send one of his to the UNDERWORLD. That's the Yu-Shan way, and that's how you get Rakan Thulio!&quot;</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2627,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2627-sleepinin","user":"Sleepinin","date":". 04-01-2014, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2627-sleepinin","name":"Sleepinin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T08:50:01-07:00","id":104072,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\">Argenthonios, God of Silver</span><br /> <br /> Argenthonios' purview is silver and he gains much of his power from the prominence of the Guild's silver standard. Potential threats to his purview include: <br /> - An Infernal Guildsman is trying to introduce a new currency to Creation. This brass standard is impossible to counterfeit and is the sole currency accepted by certain demonic cartels that have begun an aggressive expansion into Creation. If the Infernal is not dealt with, all of Creation's wealth will fall under the control of Hell.<br /> - One of the Great Houses as engineered a fad of silver art and jewelry. The value of silver has increased drastically, but it is becoming impractical as a form of currency. The jade standard is rapidly gaining ground, and it's only a matter of time before the silver fad ends.<br /> - A Solar has carved a nation out for herself and abolished all forms of currency. Her arguments are so compelling that her people are glad to labour without reward and the power of her sorcery allows her subjects to live at a much higher standard of living than they normally would. If other nations follow her example, or if she floods the market with her nation's goods, the value of the silver standard might plummet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T08:24:28-07:00","id":114724,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Siakal, Goddess of Western War, Slaughter and Sharks </span><br /> <br /> Siakal's purview includes naval warfare, wholesale slaughter and sharks. Potential threats to her purview include: <br /> - A shark-totem Lunar has set himself up as a god-king in the western archipelagos and demands to be worshiped as the God of Sharks, undermining Siakal's influence over the animals. She requires an Exalted champion of her own to remind the west who commands the ocean's most ruthless predators. <br /> - A Deathknight in the service of the Silver Prince commands fleets of immortal zombies and specters. This dread fleet swells with victory after victory, and the blood of the dead does not satisfy the thirst of Siakal. The Deathknight must be stopped before bloodless warfare dominates the West. <br /> - A Solar privateer of the Eclipse Caste has taken up a crusade against piracy, and pirates have become rarer and more timid. Worse, the Solar does not sacrifice her foes to the ocean, but presses them into legitimate service within her own fleet. The Chosen of Siakal must slaughter the Solar and all her followers to return western warfare to its proper state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T09:49:41-07:00","id":114760,"title":"","content":"The first Exigent I'm likely to do is Zhuzhiao, whom you may recall is sort of a &quot;dragon hoard&quot; octopus god of shipwrecks and the lightless depths. He jealously guards sunken treasure and will only trade for something of greater value. The default recommended hook for this exigent, I think, if you don't have anything in mind, is just &quot;someone stole something really valuable from Zhuzhiao, and he has little idea where they took it, and in any event it's likely on land where his power is diminished,&quot; because this is a pretty straightforway to get that Exigent to any part of the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the whole, I think it's more fun to come up with game-relevant stuff that might require an Exigent Exaltation, then figure out what type of Exigent it would create. So far the only thing I've come up with in this vein is an Exigent of Thorns, which I also like enough that I will probably give it a go when the book is out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 04-17-2014, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T10:00:05-07:00","id":118473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=104072#post104072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Argenthonios, God of Silver</span><br /> <br /> - A Solar has carved a nation out for herself and abolished all forms of currency. Her arguments are so compelling that her people are glad to labour without reward and the power of her sorcery allows her subjects to live at a much higher standard of living than they normally would. If other nations follow her example, or if she floods the market with her nation's goods, the value of the silver standard might plummet.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an idea that's practically dancing and singing in my head right now. Exigents have positively thrilled me since day one and this is one of the most plainly fun ideas for one of our spunky God-Champions we've seen yet. That, and Siakal's Aquaman. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2796-cthulhu_wakes","name":"Cthulhu_Wakes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T12:32:14-07:00","id":119890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=114760#post114760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first Exigent I'm likely to do is Zhuzhiao, whom you may recall is sort of a &quot;dragon hoard&quot; octopus god of shipwrecks and the lightless depths. He jealously guards sunken treasure and will only trade for something of greater value. The default recommended hook for this exigent, I think, if you don't have anything in mind, is just &quot;someone stole something really valuable from Zhuzhiao, and he has little idea where they took it, and in any event it's likely on land where his power is diminished,&quot; because this is a pretty straightforway to get that Exigent to any part of the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the whole, I think it's more fun to come up with game-relevant stuff that might require an Exigent Exaltation, then figure out what type of Exigent it would create. So far the only thing I've come up with in this vein is an Exigent of Thorns, which I also like enough that I will probably give it a go when the book is out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or perhaps one of the treasure Zhuzhiao holds IS an Exigence, hopped up full of his power. Anyone can trade him for it if they can present something of sufficient value to him for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1252,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","user":"God_of_Awesome","date":". 04-26-2014, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T08:42:23-07:00","id":120953,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Plentimon of the Dice, God of Gambling<br /> <br /> Plentimon is the god of gambling and gamblers. Threats to his purview include:<br /> - An Abyssal gambler created an artifact deck of soulsteel cards which entraps the souls of those who gamble with it and lose. The Deathknight has used this artifact to capture the souls of mortals as well as the essence of spirits... including Plentimon himself. Before his essence was sealed, the God of Gambling was able to send a portion of it out to Exalt a champion capable of outwitting the Deathknight and releasing his trapped souls. <br /> - A Night Caste gambler lost a fortune at the Diving Sea Snake Casino and skipped town before paying his debts. Plentimon has charged the Chosen of Gambling with tracking the Solar down and settling the debt for Plentimon's honour. <br /> - Plentimon keeps a ledger of his casino's wealthiest regular guests. The ledger was stolen by a Lunar looking for targets to impersonate, but Plentimon cannot disclose the theft without undermining his own reputation. He requires and Exalted champion to quietly protect the clients and recover the ledger before the Lunar cannibalizes one of them. </span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T12:23:20-07:00","id":121109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=120953#post120953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[SIZE=14px]Plentimon of the Dice, God of Gambling<br /> <br /> Plentimon is the god of gambling and gamblers. Threats to his purview include:<br /> - An Abyssal gambler created an artifact deck of soulsteel cards which entraps the souls of those who gamble with it and lose. The Deathknight has used this artifact to capture the souls of mortals as well as the essence of spirits... including Plentimon himself. Before his essence was sealed, the God of Gambling was able to send a portion of it out to Exalt a champion capable of outwitting the Deathknight and releasing his trapped souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>...And now I'm not sure if I want to play a Deadlands Huckster or a Persona protagonist, but either way the card thing is a <i>hella</i> cool hook for a spellcaster type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T17:05:26-07:00","id":121304,"title":"","content":"I myself have some Exigent character ideas.<br /> <br /> Ahlat, Southern God of War and Cattle<br /> <br /> In the First Age when the Sun started his whispers of rebellion against Those Before, Ahlat was smart, he started strife in the South among the mortals and so steeled them for the hard times to come. In war heroes are born and so many Solars exalted in the south from the flames of the wars started by Ahlat. Now in the Age of Sorrows hard times are on the way again and Ahlat like many others see it coming and have his own plans to prepare it.<br /> <br /> Ahlat has many fanatic followers among the southern people of Harborhead. Among these, the Brides of Ahlat are the most notable. He has previously championed a daughter among them that did grand things and with Exigence has the opportunity to do this again. One must gather his people against the rule of the Realm.<br /> <br /> <br /> Burning Feather, The Lady of Intoxicants<br /> <br /> The White Lady always have been known to go to lesser extremes to reach her personal goals. Take mortal lovers for as long as seasons so that enlightened children may help her further her plans, possess mortals as to stay outside the eyes of heaven. Things such as blackmail and the like is a daily endavour.<br /> <br /> Now what if something really big happened to her. Such as the drug fields of Great Forks was burned to the ground or the Realm suddenly putting a heavy ban on all intoxicants in the Riverlands? A simple godblooded child would not suffice here, and her own actions be too limited by the laws of Yu-Shan. She would need something more. Someone who can move freely and make a difference beyond mortal capabilities.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amateur drawsmith","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2847-thatsmellygoblin","name":"ThatSmellyGoblin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2847_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T20:04:43-07:00","id":188391,"title":"","content":"Just had this idea for a god. Might as well make an Exigent out of it. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Burning Winter, Broken God of the First Snows</span><br /> Cleansing Winter was once the field god of a Northern village. As part of his duties, he governed the growth and withering of the crops, the preservation of foodstocks and the fall of the first snow of each winter. However, one of the Realm's Lesser Houses sent forth its forces to subdue the village in order to create a commercial foothold in the North. A Fire Aspect sorcerer battled Cleansing Winter and horrifically mutilated the god's Essence so that the village would become dependent upon the Lesser House's assistance to cultivate its crops. Now, the snows called forth by Burning Winter burn white, searing away even the clothes of the god's victims, and leave behind a thick, noxious white fog. Burning Winter would require an Exalted Champion for one of the following tasks: <br /> - The god's existence is a thing of unspeakable suffering. He wishes to sacrifice his Essence to the Exigence simply to make the burning pain stop. <br /> - The god demands vengeance upon those who are responsible for his humiliation. He requires an Exigent to wage war against the Realm and burn the Blessed Isle until it can no longer support life. <br /> - Burning Winter wishes to return to its former self, but lacks the sorcerous knowledge to do so. He requires a champion to venture forth and recover the lost sorcery of the Celestial Circle, which will surely undo the curse of the Fire Aspect sorcerer. <br /> - A certain Sidereal has been tasked with restoring the god's proper Fate, but cannot intervene directly against the Dragonblooded sorcerer, who has somehow learned of the Chosen of the Maidens and taken appropriate precautions against them. Instead, the Sidereal has elected to nominate one of the villagers as Burning Winter's Exalted Champion, and to support her in restoring the field god's power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T21:42:16-07:00","id":188500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=114760#post114760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first Exigent I'm likely to do is Zhuzhiao, whom you may recall is sort of a &quot;dragon hoard&quot; octopus god of shipwrecks and the lightless depths. He jealously guards sunken treasure and will only trade for something of greater value. The default recommended hook for this exigent, I think, if you don't have anything in mind, is just &quot;someone stole something really valuable from Zhuzhiao, and he has little idea where they took it, and in any event it's likely on land where his power is diminished,&quot; because this is a pretty straightforway to get that Exigent to any part of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of his powers is his ability to summon up any artifact from below the waves. I was trying to figure out a way to make this an Exigent charm, letting the Exigent summon up artifacts, but it just seemed like a power that would give them too many issues and cause problems at the table. Any idea of how you're thinking of approaching that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T21:43:24-07:00","id":188501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=84557#post84557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that something we've been told? I was under the impression it was up to the God (player/ST) designing the new Exaltation if they wanted it to be a permanent thing or not...</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't know exactly what the developers have in mind, a general rule of thumb is that Exaltations are miracles created by gods neither omnipotent nor omniscient, and not devices crafted by engineers on scientific principles. Their natures and qualities, powers and limitations, are functions of narrative and mythic resonance. In short: They are as the storyteller defines them, which is not necessarily how their creators would choose to define them if they were omnipotent, omniscient, perfectly rational actors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T21:47:41-07:00","id":188502,"title":"","content":"Also: <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WYW_lPlekiQ\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WYW_lPlekiQ</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T21:52:37-07:00","id":188505,"title":"","content":"That does open the door to some weird and wild conceptions...Right now, I'm entertaining the notion of an Exigent Exaltation that starts off weak, but steadily grows in power, adding a dot to Essence a month/year, until it finally burns out its host at its maximum rating. The Exigent knows that he has but a little, limited time to accomplish his goal, before passing it on to his successor, who can hopefully succeed where he failed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T23:14:43-07:00","id":188529,"title":"","content":"One of the two exigent sets I've been working one of them are Ghouls, the chosen of Han-Tha. I was planning on setting them up almost like a zombie-plague-style. They can spread their Exaltation via biting other people. Of course, while technically &quot;Exalted&quot; being a Ghoul is very much not something you don't want to turn into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T01:43:59-07:00","id":188593,"title":"","content":"This isn't an example really of a specific one but I think one of the more important things about exigence is how it will change the setting. The 2nd edition setting did a poor job of providing other groups who had common essence use. It certainly seemed to come across in some ways that supernatural puissance meant one of two options. Either you were dealing with a Dragonblooded of some kind or Anathema. Introducing the idea of Exigents and making it at least somewhat common gives so much more options to the Celestial who desires to stay under the radar. Of course this might have been done with superior godblooded rules or setting support but those seemed to be less common than Exalted were. Just a personal feeling I got from the second edition in terms of what the options were when you encountered a human who can wield essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/BogMod\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/BogMod</a> I play a lot of videogames.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/131-bogmod","name":"BogMod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T06:54:53-07:00","id":188675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=188501#post188501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't know exactly what the developers have in mind, a general rule of thumb is that Exaltations are miracles created by gods neither omnipotent nor omniscient, and not devices crafted by engineers on scientific principles. Their natures and qualities, powers and limitations, are functions of narrative and mythic resonance. In short: They are as the storyteller defines them, which is not necessarily how their creators would choose to define them if they were omnipotent, omniscient, perfectly rational actors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mister Minton is a smart kitty! <br /> <br /> A god can't very well forge his very essence into a divine fire for humanity without, y'know, <i>putting his essence into it</i>. <br /> <br /> Also I've capitalized the first letter in &quot;Essence&quot; often enough that my phone's autocorrect recognizes that as the default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T12:34:38-07:00","id":188875,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to figure out how to do the Chosen of Artificial Flight in Heaven's Reach. Does anyone know a comprehensive book on the history of aerospace engineering?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T14:14:45-07:00","id":188928,"title":"","content":"I thought the God of Personal Tutors would be an interesting source for an Exigent - the powers could make you the ultimate sifu, drill sergeant, or sorcery tutor. Of course, you would receive the Exigence by being taught it by another Chosen of the Classroom, making the number of Exigents potentially unlimited. So you'd have to make the &quot;course&quot; last for years of full-time study, and have some uncertainty about whether you &quot;graduate&quot;. I wouldn't kill off the God, just have him lose a whole lot of power and be demoted to something like &quot;God of Inspirational Teachers of Disadvantaged Children&quot;. No idea what he'd need an Exigent for in the first place, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1430-gareth3","name":"Gareth3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T15:15:32-07:00","id":188943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gareth3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=188928#post188928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the God of Personal Tutors would be an interesting source for an Exigent - the powers could make you the ultimate sifu, drill sergeant, or sorcery tutor. Of course, you would receive the Exigence by being taught it by another Chosen of the Classroom, making the number of Exigents potentially unlimited. So you'd have to make the &quot;course&quot; last for years of full-time study, and have some uncertainty about whether you &quot;graduate&quot;. I wouldn't kill off the God, just have him lose a whole lot of power and be demoted to something like &quot;God of Inspirational Teachers of Disadvantaged Children&quot;. No idea what he'd need an Exigent for in the first place, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps a political gambit?<br /> &quot;I lose a lot of power <i>now</i>, but I happen to live <i>forever</i> and, with some political maneuvering and my Exalted spreading my portfolio of training and education far and wide, I can become a true powerhouse in Yu-Shan! Maybe even vie for the position of Head of the Bureau of Humanity! Oh, the power, the Influence, the Ambrosia!...and the humans would advance and live better too, I guess.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T15:32:38-07:00","id":188946,"title":"","content":"Yeah, something like that. The propagation of the Exigence might be slow, but if it's Celestial-level and enough students manage to graduate, it could eventually be massively powerful. Actual mechanics would have to wait for Third Edition, but I have a few ideas for charms. You could make training times instant for anything you could conventionally teach, enlighten Dragon Kings instantly, and detect any Ability that someone else learnt from a personal tutor. Maybe you could even teach sorcery spells and martial arts you don't even know, or train people to abilities beyond your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1430-gareth3","name":"Gareth3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T20:46:21-07:00","id":189902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=120953#post120953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Plentimon of the Dice, God of Gambling<br /> <br /> Plentimon is the god of gambling and gamblers. Threats to his purview include:<br /> - An Abyssal gambler created an artifact deck of soulsteel cards which entraps the souls of those who gamble with it and lose. The Deathknight has used this artifact to capture the souls of mortals as well as the essence of spirits... including Plentimon himself. Before his essence was sealed, the God of Gambling was able to send a portion of it out to Exalt a champion capable of outwitting the Deathknight and releasing his trapped souls.. </span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Jojo's Bizarre Adventures?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The only thing I'm not liking here are the Soulsteel cards...I think we sometimes forget that Soulsteel is a bottomless void in the shape of an object, blacker than the blackest black. You wouldn't be able to see what cards you were playing with!<br /> <br /> Cards made of human skin, with actual bone detailing might work. Better yet, have this be done by an upgrade to that Ink Monkey gambling charm (the one I'm pretty sure must have been inspired by <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gonna_Roll_the_Bones\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Gonna Roll the Bones&quot;</a>)!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T20:48:28-07:00","id":189904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThatSmellyGoblin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=121304#post121304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ahlat has many fanatic followers among the southern people of Harborhead. Among these, the Brides of Ahlat are the most notable. He has previously championed a daughter among them that did grand things and with Exigence has the opportunity to do this again. One must gather his people against the rule of the Realm.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm...How would you all feel if 3E retconned Ahlat's daughter, Blood-on-the-Horn, into being an Exigent instead? It would show how they have shaped the world...but would it take away from God-Bloods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T20:59:10-07:00","id":189906,"title":"","content":"I think it'd just be... <i>off</i> for Ahlat. The connection between the Brides of Ahlat and the Exigents is just so obvious that I don't think Ahlat would Exalt one of his children. <br /> <br /> Now, if Blood-on-the-Horn was retconned into one of Ahlat's Brides, then it would make more sense for her to be the Chosen of Southern War. It'd probably still be weird though, what with the history she already has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T06:50:18-07:00","id":190235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=188501#post188501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't know exactly what the developers have in mind, a general rule of thumb is that Exaltations are miracles created by gods neither omnipotent nor omniscient, and not devices crafted by engineers on scientific principles. Their natures and qualities, powers and limitations, are functions of narrative and mythic resonance. In short: They are as the storyteller defines them, which is not necessarily how their creators would choose to define them if they were omnipotent, omniscient, perfectly rational actors.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the record, even if they were devices crafted by engineers working from scientific principles, they're still constrained by their materials, personal capabilities and personalities, and by the fact that you only get to invoke this thing once, so no testing cycle.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I could totally buy that a non-human intelligence working with arcane components to a set of priorities based on current needs and predilections, to a set of rules they don't necessarily fully understand would produce something which, after hundreds of years, people would look at and go &quot;What the heck?!? Why did they do that?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T21:21:08-07:00","id":191093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=188875#post188875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to figure out how to do the Chosen of Artificial Flight in Heaven's Reach. Does anyone know a comprehensive book on the history of aerospace engineering?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but I do know Kang the Mad. How much more inspiration could you possibly need? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nztPLExhOlU\" data-code=\"nztPLExhOlU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/nztPLExhOlU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">(And that's not even the half of it...)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T16:04:19-07:00","id":253650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThatSmellyGoblin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=121304#post121304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Burning Feather, The Lady of Intoxicants<br /> <br /> The White Lady always have been known to go to lesser extremes to reach her personal goals. Take mortal lovers for as long as seasons so that enlightened children may help her further her plans, possess mortals as to stay outside the eyes of heaven. Things such as blackmail and the like is a daily endavour.<br /> <br /> Now what if something really big happened to her. Such as the drug fields of Great Forks was burned to the ground or the Realm suddenly putting a heavy ban on all intoxicants in the Riverlands? A simple godblooded child would not suffice here, and her own actions be too limited by the laws of Yu-Shan. She would need something more. Someone who can move freely and make a difference beyond mortal capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a Solar take over the Northern Slave States and release the population from their drug-addled slavery. This is a perfect idea to raise as opposition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/566-the-third-fetich","name":"The Third Fetich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T10:54:12-07:00","id":254209,"title":"","content":"Five Days Darkness would probably want one, though I'd doubt they would be as Solar-like as he hopes. <br /> <br /> ALL-MIGHTY ORICALCUM CHIEF- One of the more influential gods of Yu-Shan, the egotistical and vain spirit's domain as the god of Cookery allows him huge capital in the hedonistic city of heaven. Never the less, he remains aloft from his peers, his dedication to his art overpowering even his pride. While harsh to those who he feels are not up to snuff, he is fair in his ruthlessness, and will(reluctantly) heap praise on those who prove worthy. While a Exigent would make the perfect errand boy, he has more pressing matters to attend to. For, since the loss of the First Age, the art of Cookery has grown weak in Creation. What is called fine today would be peasent food then, and people then would starve rather than eat what peasents eat in the Broken Age. With the return of the Lawgivers, he now sees his chance. Go forth, he tells his champion, and make a world worthy of the finest meals! Alternativly, he might view hunger as a personal offense, and bid his chosen to rid Creation of such Blasphemy. Likely abilities include Melee, Performance, Craft(Water, if they keep them divided), Socialize, and Resistance. <br /> <br /> TEN THOUSAND BEETLE WHISPERS- The god of Insects is a ...unnerving individual. Many mortals with just enough knowledge assume him to be one of the Forbidden due to his unfortunate tendency to appear as a giant swarm of insects arranged in an almost human form. Never the less, while he is in no way the best conversationalist, he is benevoltent enough, and has a mortal bride with whom he is shockingly faithful. He is also a good friend of the Manse of Ivy, possessing an honorary position for his skill in obtaining the knowledge few others can. <br /> Exigent possibilities: <br /> <br /> \u2022An important Sidereal fact-finding mission needs a public, Exalted face who knows enough to not be a hinderance while still being both powerful and, if it comes down to it, disposable. Beetle has volunteered his own Essence to provide aid at the behest of a Chosen of Secrets he has befriended. <br /> <br /> \u2022 A Loyalist Abyssal has started advertising himself to many towns and villages with a disease that only kills insects. Many are buying his product, eager to be rid of pests, unaware of how badly this could disturb the local ecology. Whispers will need a champion to stop the Herald of Oblivion before any major damages occurs. <br /> <br /> \u2022Someone has captured Whispers's wife and daughter in order to manipulate him in some game of politics. He has responded by Chosing someone with a grudge against the kipnapper and offering them all the pull they need to make him HURT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T23:42:41-07:00","id":255087,"title":"","content":"The hard part for me is coming up with greater deities for whom an Exigent is clearly a distinct choice from some other kind of Celestial Exalted character concept. Like Ruvia - how is a Chosen of Roads thematically distinct from a Chosen of Journeys enough for me to bother designing a new charmset for this character? How are most Chosen of [War God] not going to just be &quot;Lesser Dawn&quot; or &quot;Lesser Chosen of Battles?&quot;<br /> <br /> I wonder how anti-predetermination oriented the Chosen of Plentimon is going to be... or is that Luranume's territory?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T01:44:43-07:00","id":255139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=255087#post255087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hard part for me is coming up with greater deities for whom an Exigent is clearly a distinct choice from some other kind of Celestial Exalted character concept. Like Ruvia - how is a Chosen of Roads thematically distinct from a Chosen of Journeys enough for me to bother designing a new charmset for this character? How are most Chosen of [War God] not going to just be &quot;Lesser Dawn&quot; or &quot;Lesser Chosen of Battles?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that why exigent's only supposed to be for gods of physical objects and not concepts?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T01:50:47-07:00","id":255141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=255139#post255139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that why exigent's only supposed to be for gods of physical objects and not concepts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First I've heard of such a restriction! I'm 88% sure it's been said that Plentimon is getting a canonical Exigent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T01:52:54-07:00","id":255142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=84661#post84661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on the Strawmaiden Janest fiction, gods need to pray to the Unconquered Sun to be able to use the Exigence</div> </div> </div> </div>Legal ones anyway. We know blackmarket Exigence is a thing - and is one of the new problems Sidereals have on their plate this edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T01:57:39-07:00","id":255143,"title":"","content":"I don't really think a Harvest count as a physical object.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T09:23:12-07:00","id":255351,"title":"","content":"Has anyone here read the Wheel of Time? I think Mat Cauthon would be a perfect Exigent for Plentimon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T09:01:47-07:00","id":256080,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Luxana, Goddess of Recorded Knowledge</span></b><br /> <br /> Luxana, the prim and proper goddess of the written word, works in the Division of Secrets. Every disaster in the Time of Tumult sets back the amount of human knowledge and decreases the level of literacy in Creation, which directly threatens her purview. To prevent this, she has created the first of her Archival Exalted from one of her Scroll Maidens<span style=\"font-size:14px\"> and tasked her with these objectives:</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Find and preserve ancient long-lost stores of learning, from caches of Dragon King crystal records, to the great libraries of the First Age. Special notice is given to the Library of Sperimen, which must be freed from the Queen of Fangs (unless she can be persuaded to allow its general use to those who would seek its knowledge).</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Aid those of scholarly bent (Twilights, No Moons, Scavenger Lords), and oppose those who would destroy the learning of civilization (barbarian Lunars, Fair Folk, Amoth City-Smiter and his minions). </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Encourage the growth of progressive city-states and their libraries and universities, such as in Nexus. Convince other city-states of the benefits of organized learning. </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Apocalypse Scrolls have been stolen from Heaven! Luxana must act quickly and discreetly to recover them before the Division loses face, and even the Chosen of the Maidens can't be trusted with this mission...</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Entire libraries full of priceless knowledge and writing have been lost over the eons...however, their shadows still linger in the Underworld. The Archival Exalted must dare the Underworld itself to search these shadowy, labyrinthine buildings, many crawling with all manner of monsters, and find a way to bring the plasmic volumes back into Creation. </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The behemoth Halkomelem, spawned by He Who Bleeds the Unknown Word, is a hundred-yard long serpent made of crimson paper covered in golden script. The pages he sheds contains many lost works and secrets known only to the Yozis. The Archival must brave hell to gather enough scale-pages to bind into a new book, containing information vital to the safety of Creation.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Though it grieves Luxana, there is some knowledge which must never come to light, and some books must be suppressed for the good of all. Chief among these is the Broken-Winged Crane, which the Archival must ever be on the look out for. But many other cursed and forbidden tomes exist, and these must be found and either destroyed or locked away deep within the Forbidding Manse of Ivy or the Malachite Archives in Yu-Shan. </span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Pictured: The First of the Archival Exalted</i></span><br /> <img src=\"http://mimi1380.m.i.pic.centerblog.net/9nq606ln.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 09-13-2014, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T09:54:39-07:00","id":256112,"title":"","content":"Hand, isn't Amoth City-Smiter the god of bribery? What's that got anything to do with reducing literacy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T10:47:45-07:00","id":256138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=256112#post256112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hand, isn't Amoth City-Smiter the god of bribery? What's that got anything to do with reducing literacy?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Technically, but he is also the God of Tumbled Ruins, and secretly works with barbarians, Lunars and Raksha to destroy cities and towns, and civilization in general. The Dogs of the Unbroken Earth report to him and he actively attacks Scavenger Lords and others who would rebuild or save things from ruins, including knowledge. <br /> <br /> I thought the God of Bribery was that one dude, who's a mass of serpents in humanoid form, but he's actually the God of Blackmail (also, he's compromised by the Ebon Dragon)!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T00:29:00-07:00","id":261147,"title":"","content":"Awesome posts, Tiresias.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=114724#post114724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Siakal, Goddess of Western War, Slaughter and Sharks </span><br /> <br /> Siakal's purview includes naval warfare, wholesale slaughter and sharks. Potential threats to her purview include:<br /> - A shark-totem Lunar has set himself up as a god-king in the western archipelagos and demands to be worshiped as the God of Sharks, undermining Siakal's influence over the animals. She requires an Exalted champion of her own to remind the west who commands the ocean's most ruthless predators.<br /> - A Deathknight in the service of the Silver Prince commands fleets of immortal zombies and specters. This dread fleet swells with victory after victory, and the blood of the dead does not satisfy the thirst of Siakal. The Deathknight must be stopped before bloodless warfare dominates the West.<br /> - A Solar privateer of the Eclipse Caste has taken up a crusade against piracy, and pirates have become rarer and more timid. Worse, the Solar does not sacrifice her foes to the ocean, but presses them into legitimate service within her own fleet. The Chosen of Siakal must slaughter the Solar and all her followers to return western warfare to its proper state.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Note how for the most part, Siakal's reasons for wanting an Exigent would be illegal as shit and would get her four thumbs down from the Unconquered Sun. What you are often listing are reasons why the gods try to get a hold of &quot;black market&quot; Exaltations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T00:33:32-07:00","id":261148,"title":"","content":"Ahlat is another good example of the Unconquered Sun laughing at a god's request. <br /> <br /> Re: Autochthon: The Unconquered Sun created the Exigence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T01:11:52-07:00","id":261151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=255087#post255087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hard part for me is coming up with greater deities for whom an Exigent is clearly a distinct choice from some other kind of Celestial Exalted character concept. Like Ruvia - how is a Chosen of Roads thematically distinct from a Chosen of Journeys enough for me to bother designing a new charmset for this character? How are most Chosen of [War God] not going to just be &quot;Lesser Dawn&quot; or &quot;Lesser Chosen of Battles?&quot;<br /> <br /> I wonder how anti-predetermination oriented the Chosen of Plentimon is going to be... or is that Luranume's territory?</div> </div> </div> </div>We have an Exigent of a major road god planned. I would never have even thought to make the comparison to a Sidereal, his powers are that different. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T02:01:12-07:00","id":261161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=255087#post255087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how anti-predetermination oriented the Chosen of Plentimon is going to be... or is that Luranume's territory?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea was that I had for how Plentimon's Chosen could be very different from Luranume's was that they would embrace and embody a lot of gambler's superstitions like the idea that having a run of bad luck means you're more likely to win next time or that needing the money for a worthy cause makes you more likely to win, not anathema to the notion of destiny but viewing it like the Heart of the Cards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 09-20-2014, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T06:10:46-07:00","id":261225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=261147#post261147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note how for the most part, Siakal's reasons for wanting an Exigent would be illegal as shit and would get her four thumbs down from the Unconquered Sun. What you are often listing are reasons why the gods try to get a hold of &quot;black market&quot; Exaltations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am intrigued. I tried to come up with motivations that would gain the Unconquered Sun's approval on the basis that they're directly related to a threat to the gods' purviews, rather than the gods' desire to simply expand their influence in some way. <br /> <br /> So I would guess that the Unconquered Sun answers praying for the Exigence depending on how the gods' interests intersect with mortal interests?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T11:29:04-07:00","id":261370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=261151#post261151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We have an Exigent of a major road god planned. I would never have even thought to make the comparison to a Sidereal, his powers are that different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm psyched for this, since I always felt that road gods were underutilized territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T11:43:26-07:00","id":264006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=261225#post261225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am intrigued. I tried to come up with motivations that would gain the Unconquered Sun's approval on the basis that they're directly related to a threat to the gods' purviews, rather than the gods' desire to simply expand their influence in some way.<br /> <br /> So I would guess that the Unconquered Sun answers praying for the Exigence depending on how the gods' interests intersect with mortal interests?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not quite. It has more to do with virtuosity than pragmatism. Don't change your ideas, though. Keep going, you are doing great posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T15:30:34-07:00","id":264171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=189904#post189904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm...How would you all feel if 3E retconned Ahlat's daughter, Blood-on-the-Horn, into being an Exigent instead? It would show how they have shaped the world...but would it take away from God-Bloods?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope they don't.<br /> <br /> After rereading Houses of the Bull God this is now my preferred way to add Exigence to that narrative.<ul><li>Ahlat applies for Exigence so that his Chosen could unite Harborhead, he is denied.</li> <li>Ahlat sires Blood-on-the-Horn who goes onto do what his Exigent would've done.</li> <li>The Realm unable to ignore the situation send 6 legions and Blood-on-the-Horn is killed in single combat.</li> <li>Enraged Ahlat confronts Taichi-Kun in Yu-Shan it's a tense moment as the two war gods square off until the Unconquered Sun intervenes.</li> <li>Once they're alone he speaks to Ahlat about why his earlier request for Exigence was denied, it's very much a conversation between old friends and during this he talks about his own experiences as a father and mentions the Solar Exalted. Ahlat understands.</li> <li>He offers him the Exigence that was declined him 60 years earlier knowing he could easily use it to get revenge on Tachi-Kun.</li> </ul><br /> 346 years later Ahlat still keeps the Exigence in a safe place. He's been tempted to use it several times over the centuries before ultimately deciding it's unnecessary. But as the Time of Tumult worsens he may soon have no choice but to Exalt a champion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T15:38:14-07:00","id":264197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=264171#post264171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope they don't.<br /> <br /> After rereading Houses of the Bull God this is now my preferred way to add Exigence to that narrative.<ul><li>Ahlat applies for Exigence so that his Chosen could unite Harborhead, he is denied.</li> <li>Ahlat sires Blood-on-the-Horn who goes onto do what his Exigent would've done.</li> <li>The Realm unable to ignore the situation send 6 legions and Blood-on-the-Horn is killed in single combat.</li> <li>Enraged Ahlat confronts Taichi-Kun in Yu-Shan it's a tense moment as the two war gods square off until the Unconquered Sun intervenes.</li> <li>Once they're alone he speaks to Ahlat about why his earlier request for Exigence was denied, it's very much a conversation between old friends and during this he talks about his own experiences as a father and mentions the Solar Exalted. Ahlat understands.</li> <li>He offers him the Exigence that was declined him 60 years earlier knowing he could easily use it to get revenge on Tachi-Kun.</li> </ul><br /> 346 years later Ahlat still keeps the Exigence in a safe place. He's been tempted to use it several times over the centuries before ultimately deciding it's unnecessary. But as the Time of Tumult worsens he may soon have no choice but to Exalt a champion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe make the Exigent Blood-On-The-Horn'r reincarnation? Make it pleasing to both crowds and add some &quot;living in the shadow of&quot; narative?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T15:52:04-07:00","id":264206,"title":"","content":"Consider that idea stolen, Lioness - that was beautiful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T16:08:02-07:00","id":264219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=264197#post264197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe make the Exigent Blood-On-The-Horn'r reincarnation? Make it pleasing to both crowds and add some &quot;living in the shadow of&quot; narative?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or decedent. Blood-On-The-Horn was 60 when she died, it wouldn't exactly be out of left field if she'd already had kids.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 09-24-2014, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T19:44:26-07:00","id":264353,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking of doing a Zhuzhiao exigent, because it seems like a strong palette to work with, and my current thinking for that is that the default justification would be that someone powerful stole some sort of game-specific MacGuffin from Zhuzhiao's horde, and then ran off with it to a place where Zhuzhiao couldn't reach. It's a little pedestrian, but it gives you an in to play the character in any part of the world, and you can easily wire it into an ongoing plot, like you're in a game about fighting the Dowager and your character's goal is to track down the Dowager, punch her in the face, take the Collar of Broken Dreams back from her, and huck it in the ocean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T02:22:42-07:00","id":265295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=264006#post264006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite. It has more to do with virtuosity than pragmatism.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes a lot of sense.<br /> Its easier to avoid having a watered down version of an existing Exalt type if you're encouraged to think of the god in question as a sentient being with dimensions to their personality rather than a robot who only wants to advance their purview. Especially when you've got Black Market Exigents for when the purview is more than enough to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T13:11:47-07:00","id":284107,"title":"","content":"MUCALINDA- SHOGUN OF SHAMANS, DAIYMO OF SERPENTS, AND SUB-ADMINISTRATOR OF HARVESTS, HEALTH, AND INTOXICANTS. <br /> Mucalinda was not always so grand as he is today. No, before the Primordial war, he was little but a lesser god of a eastern species of snakes. But, by hook and by crook, he has raised himself into one of the more influential spirits in Yu-Shan, using his political acumen, skills at deception, and weak prophetic abilities to outmaneuver his opponents. A good portion of his power comes from being the direct subordinate of(and ambassador between) three rather potent spirits in the court of Yu-Shan. In terms of appearance, he usually takes the form of a Snakeman of some kind, often related to some Eastern species, to reflect the fondness for the direction in which he &quot;grew up&quot;. Since his recent adoption of the Naga, a group of patronless rain gods, he has started taking a form in homage of their own, an 7 ft upright, four armed snake whose tail is a tangle of venomous serpents. He can take a more human form, but no matter what shape he takes, his eyes are always the cold slivers of his serpent charges. He tends to the cold and calculating, often seeing his fellow gods(such as his yes-man and crony, the god of eastern dragonflies) as nothing more than tools, to be discarded at a whim. Never the less, he does try to do what he thinks is best for his worshipers and charges, even if he is prone to think of them more as pets than people. He also bears genuine respect for those who seek to rise above their station, as he once did, and those who are truly devout, no matter what they believe(that is not to say he will tolerate the servants of Oblivion or the Yozi; rather, he will ensure the poison that melts away their insides suppresses their pain rather than enhancing it). He is relatively skilled at Martial Arts, though he is no great master. He is notable for teaching the art of hand-to-hand combat to the Solar who would invent Snake style. He often appears somewhat mystical to outsiders, prone to keeping secrets and using hallucinogenics alongside his panoply charms to gain vague insights into the future. Likely Abilities for his Chosen include Brawl and Dodge(the snake is swift and deadly, striking fast and escaping gracefully as its venom finishes its foe ), Socialize(The Daimyo of Serpents is a skilled manipulator, and snakes are well-known for deceit and desire), Survival and Medicine(Serpents are symbols of health and fertility the world over), and Occult(Serpents often have mystical and deathly associations, not to mention the prophetic might of the Shogun of Shamans himself). <br /> REASONS FOR EXIGENCE <br /> \u2022 Mucalinda is seething with rage. A growing number of his eastern followers have been tortured, killed, and enslaved by House Cynis, who have been using them to harvest the sacred plants used by the tribe's shamans in many important rituals. While he might have shown them mercy if they wished to partake in the wisdom brought by the magical intoxicant, they have merely grown tired of the current drug de jour and only want to find a novel way to get high. Thus, he has sought out a Heroic enemy of the Dynasts, and has offered him power,so long as he frees the worshipers of the Snake Daimyo in the course of destroying all Cynis holds dear. <br /> \u2022Mucalinda has one responsibility he does not speak of: he is guardian of the Root-Eater Key, the only thing that can open the prison holding the Behemoth Nilbog, created by the Primordials to destroy Creation should they even grow irredeemably tired of it, the key to the prison stolen by a Night with the aid of the Great Maker, who forged the prison, just before the war. Except now the Key has been stolen! He knows not how, for he cannot remember the incident, and so he needs a champion who can look for it discretely, lest a panic be caused. <br /> \u2022 The Shogun of Serpents has sent a missive to a randomly select set of Heroic mortals in Creation, offering a mysterious prize to whichever rises highest above their current station in a year. He will then promptly Exalt the winner with no obligations, save the knowledge that to act against Creation or threaten his charges will invite the wrath of the Lord of Nagas. <br /> \u2022Mucalinda has grow annoyed with the Immaculate Faith. While he tolerates those who are truly devout, he can not tolerate how this false religion leaves mortals content with their disgusting lowliness. He therefore has scouted out a strong-willed, rebellious mortal, whom he offers an Exaltation and a mission: Do as you please, and, in doing so, spread the doctrine of ambition and desire to all of Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T13:42:39-07:00","id":294096,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Ten Thousand Spears, God of Large Armies</span></span><br /> <br /> Ten Thousand Spears is the God if Large Armies and the patron of the Realm's legions. Possible threats to his purview include:<br /> - Ten Thousand Spears has struck a deal with the Bronze faction. He will provide an Exalted champion to serve as a neutral party to command the Realm's armies against Solar-led armies in the threshold. In exchange, the Sidereals will support his attempt to usurp Tachi-Kun's position. He need only find a suitable candidate.<br /> - The battles and duels between the Dragon-Blooded warriors of the Realm Civil War are strengthening the influence of Tachi-Kun as the God of Exalted Warfare. In order to undermine his superior's position, Ten Thousand Spears has Exalted a champion to lead a populist revolt against the Dragon-Blooded and introduce a new faction into the war.<br /> - The Realm's withdrawal from the threshold is undermining its influence. Ten Thousand Spears has chosen to find a champion to unite the abandoned satrapies under a single banner to repel Lunar raids and enforce their loyalty to the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T20:35:09-07:00","id":294488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=261148#post261148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Re: Autochthon: The Unconquered Sun created the Exigence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mythologically he's never been depicted as the crafter or creator, he's been a defender and a destroyer, so I don't see how it makes sense he created the Exigence. Apparently there's a connection with Solars and sorcerous power now so maybe there is some connection there. Not sure how I feel about it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T20:37:58-07:00","id":294489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=294488#post294488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mythologically he's never been depicted as the crafter or creator, he's been a defender and a destroyer, so I don't see how it makes sense he created the Exigence. Apparently there's a connection with Solars and sorcerous power now so maybe there is some connection there. Not sure how I feel about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The creator of the Solar Exalted doesn't make sense as the creator of the Exigence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T20:42:32-07:00","id":294494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=294488#post294488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mythologically he's never been depicted as the crafter or creator, he's been a defender and a destroyer, so I don't see how it makes sense he created the Exigence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Autochthon's role as the setting's chief artisan is massively bloated, especially where Exaltations are concerned, and I'm not sure how much of it is actually canon and how much of it is pure fandom. <br /> <br /> Just because Autochthon created some things does not mean he created every single thing ever. There's room for the Unconquered Sun to act as a creator and craftsman. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T10:31:53-08:00","id":305919,"title":"","content":"<b>Hexxus, Shogun of Pollution </b><br /> -Should anything happen to the Emissary then Nexus would need a new protector and who better than one of his Chosen?<br /> -Tales of these so called &quot;Planeteers&quot; has alarmed Hexxus and forced his hand.<br /> -Someone must complete his holy book &quot;An Inconvenient Truth&quot; which currently consists only of super villainesque rantings about Carbon Footprints.<br /> -He wants to share his Toxic Love with Creation.<br /> <br /> ..Sorry. This did start out as a semi-serious idea.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T12:49:38-08:00","id":306053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=294488#post294488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mythologically he's never been depicted as the crafter or creator, he's been a defender and a destroyer, so I don't see how it makes sense he created the Exigence. Apparently there's a connection with Solars and sorcerous power now so maybe there is some connection there. Not sure how I feel about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>He gave the Essence for the Twilights as well as the Dawns and Zeniths, and considering this edition seems big on &quot;your power is your patron's power&quot;, it seems even more logical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T18:21:04-08:00","id":402691,"title":"","content":"<br /> Tien Yu knows that Lookshy's fall has been weaved in the threads by the pattern spiders, that it's end is destiny. She fights as long as she can but as she fights she depletes her city and may become a god of lost city much like her father. In a desperate gambit that burned away a lot of the time towards Lookshy's future she got an exigence to create a fate immune champion to try to change the destiny of her city. This is gamble, this is her putting everything on the line but she hopes that the reputation for exalted to make the impossible possible can hold out and set you as soldier to fight with her for Lookshy to let it survive and possibly flourish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T18:27:54-08:00","id":402703,"title":"","content":"Exalts aren't immune to fate. That's like saying they're immune to time, gravity, or Essence.<br /> <br /> And if her greatest powers come at the cost of damage to Lookshy's destiny, it will probably be true of any Exigent she makes, considering the nature of the Exigence.<br /> <br /> Moreover, it feels inappropriate for her to empower her Exigent by hastening the day of Lookshy's doom; the personal sacrifice to draw on the divine power should lessen <i>her</i>, rather than her passing the buck off onto a city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-11-2015, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T00:39:51-08:00","id":403095,"title":"","content":"Generally, I'm inclined to think that for high essence gods in general, creating Exigents is not necessarily high on their list of emergency options. Since creating a legitimate exigent is supposed to be in alignment with your actual duties somehow in many cases its probably easier for a powerful god to engage the problem personally (or through a powerful subordinate) rather than sacrifice a portion of their being to create a servant to do it. Tien Yu, for example, has any number of dragon-blooded she can ask to do just about anything she considers important.<br /> <br /> Utilizing the exigence just seems like a desperate (or in the case of black-market exaltations super high risk gamble) type of move. To again use Tien Yu as an example, there is nothing she lacks the power to beat up that an exigent would be able to stop without decades of development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1j0RQNTrhSQVIjBJw3555qA1S9Hih1SRwychiPhEwm9k/pub\" target=\"_blank\">Whitescrub Tundra Project</a>: a fan-made setting reference for Exalted 3e.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10769032/1/\" target=\"_blank\">Edge of Underleaves</a> A pair of dragon-blooded dare the jungles of the southwest.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4060-mechalich","name":"Mechalich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4060_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T01:14:01-08:00","id":403100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=402703#post402703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalts aren't immune to fate. That's like saying they're immune to time, gravity, or Essence.<br /> <br /> And if her greatest powers come at the cost of damage to Lookshy's destiny, it will probably be true of any Exigent she makes, considering the nature of the Exigence.<br /> <br /> Moreover, it feels inappropriate for her to empower her Exigent by hastening the day of Lookshy's doom; the personal sacrifice to draw on the divine power should lessen <i>her</i>, rather than her passing the buck off onto a city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tien Yu's powers arbitrarily hastening Lookshy's approaching doom was always stupid anyway, what other deity in the series has to ruin their own domain to activate their powers and defend their domain? It is a stupid piece of Catch-22 BS that nobody else has to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T03:26:40-08:00","id":403139,"title":"","content":"I don't mind charms that mess up the domain when they're trying to keep to a specific narrative like Lookshy's doom, but reducing the number of day towards a nameless doom is too invisible a cost for those charms because nobody knows how meaningful that is.<br /> These charms also only really lend themselves to one story, where they fall into the wrong hands and someone besides her can sacrifice Lookshy's remaining days.<br /> <br /> Now to try and steer the subject back to Exigence.<br /> I've personally always viewed Tien Yu as having long since absorbed the Gunzosha into her purview and embodies the idea of self-sacrifice for victory as well as the idea of diminishing stockpiles of First Age weapons. <br /> <br /> As for trying to defy fate, I see the attempt going down like this - <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dinobot</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question that once haunted my being has been answered. The future is not fixed, and my choices are my own. And yet, how ironic... for I now find that I have no choice at all! I am a warrior... let the battle be joined.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T05:09:23-08:00","id":403188,"title":"","content":"Ten Sheaves made Janest Exalted to do what he could not. I'd think the same would be true of Tien Yu.<br /> <br /> Thinking about Tien Yu's decline related powers, being linked to inevitable decline is a bit odd because, like Lioness observed, yes, the decline of the city is still whenever you feel like it, so in practice its as cosmetic a details as the Sidereal Burn Life Charm which (clearly) inspired it.<br /> <br /> Some trade of power over the destiny of the city for immediate power could work - astrological curses become easier, astrological blessings become harder. But I don't think that works too well, as adding difficulty to astrology for the whole city (or really even any part of it) on a permanent basis is too large a cost for any power, and only comes up as a real cost when Sidereals are around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T07:02:50-08:00","id":403266,"title":"","content":"This is why I'd prefer future gods with decline related powers not be linked to some non-descript doom.<br /> <br /> For example the god of an ancient walled city wears similar looking armour right down to the same crack left over from some ancient war that's become the wall's most distinctive feature. Enemies of the city state have focused their attacks upon the crack in the past to no apparent effect but the vulnerablity is no less real and unless someone versed in First Age building techniques can fix the wall it wall fall eventually. The city gods panoply includes a charm that redirects damage from them onto the wall that they've become increasingly more and more fearful of using.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T09:26:48-08:00","id":403377,"title":"","content":"MA'II, THE LAUGHING TUMBLEWEED VAGABOND-CHIEF VAGRANT, KEEPER OF COYOTES, AND TENDER OF TUMBLEWEEDS<br /> Ma'ii is a strange figure. The Laughing Tumbleweed Vagabond cares little for the politicking of his fellows up in Yu-Shan. Instead, the god of wanders, coyotes, and tumbleweeds travel around the South(primarily the South-East), watching over his charges first hand. The Chief Vagrant is a charismatic, carefree individual, whose natural charm often makes up for the fact he prefers to appear as a mangy, starving looking Southern man with the head of a coyote, though he will take a more mundane shape if the need arrives. In the mind of the Tender of Tumbleweeds, nothing is greater than freedom. Society builds chains of expectations and obligations that crush the spirit and stifles the soul; only by limiting one's attachments and traveling the world may one know their true self. He is quite friendly, caring nothing for status or rank, though he is crass and prone to cruel pranks to those he finds obnoxious. Often in areas he travels, the locals treat all guests with kindness and courtesy, for he is quick to reward good treatment with blessings, and bad treatments with horrific curses. Likely abilities for his Chosen include Survival(wanderers, coyotes, and tumbleweeds alike travel through the wilderness more often than they'd prefer), Resistance(those who wander through the desert, be they man or beast, must often go without food, water, or rest), Performance(the ability that covers the traveler's wild stories and the coyote's mournful howls), Linguistics and Socialize(knowing the local tongue can mean life or death), and Athletics(wether you've angered the local authorities or need to get to shelter quick, athletic talent is a must).<br /> REASONS FOR EXIGENCE<br /> \u2022 The Laughing Tumbleweed Vagabond is concerned. Zombies and War Ghosts have become common, attacking travelers in order to raise their numbers. People have begun hiding in cities, submitting themselves to tyrants and obligations to avoid death. This cannot stand! So now a Chosen of Ma'ii wanders Creation, dispatching the undead to make the roads and wilderness safe for travelers once again.<br /> \u2022 The Keeper of Coyotes is horrified. A wicked Exalt, allied to the souls of the Principal of Hierarchy, has staked out a territory in Creation , and plans to spread his rule throughout the world. His goal? Turn all of Creation into a single, massive city, its inhabitants turned into mindless drones who are defined by their obligations and duties. Ma'ii seeks to employ a Chosen post haste, lest freedom and travel be excised from the world!<br /> \u2022 While Ma'ii was traveling Creation, he logged in the home of a young mortal.He was impressed by their willingness to put up with his antics and to give the wandering god whatever he asked. But what really tugged at his heart was their sorry state. They were a living pawn, so bound up in obligations and duties and pre-arranged events that they had no control over their own life. When he returned to Yu-Shan, Ma'ii knew what he had to do. And so the young mortal received a gift, the greatest the Laughing Tumbleweed Vagabond could conceive: Freedom, and with it, the power to control their own destiny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T13:20:44-08:00","id":403615,"title":"","content":"Is there a god of God-bloods or hybrids, that were given names at least? I'd be curious about an exigent made from a god like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T14:58:18-08:00","id":403735,"title":"","content":"I believe that the closest to what you describe is Parad, the Left Hand of Power who is officially about Inherited Might but God Blooded fall under this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-13-2015, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T10:11:03-08:00","id":404655,"title":"","content":"I dunno how on-topic this is, but I had an idea for an Exigent. Their patron was a God of Treasure and Artiface, who had grown weaker with the decline of Creation's economy. So the God wanted a champion to bring the treasures of the First Age back to the fore, which might rekindle his Essence in ways that would even offset the Law of Diminishment somewhat. (Note: In a 'net gain' sense. The God would still be much weaker than if he had not granted the Exigence AND Creation started mass archeological digs, but was weak due to so much of the past being lost that he engaged in a desperate gamble)<br /> <br /> The resulting Exigent would be a metaphorical god among Scavenger Lords. 99% non-combat charms, for things like appraisal, mapping, and dungeon diving. Any combat skill would come from an affinity for artifact weapons, including the ability to unlock an artifact's Evocations. I don't know how viable or balanced that would be in Ex3, but I just love the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T20:22:30-08:00","id":405426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=294494#post294494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Autochthon's role as the setting's chief artisan is massively bloated, especially where Exaltations are concerned, and I'm not sure how much of it is actually canon and how much of it is pure fandom.</div> </div> </div> </div>So much so that the books themselves take a jab at it with the Pelagials, who in their first contacts with the Deliberative, centuries after Autochthon's departure, claimed to be creations of Great Maker as a convenient lie to cover the actual fact that a Primordial turned Neverborn spawned them - and they still served it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T14:12:30-07:00","id":452011,"title":"","content":"I was saving this until my players found out about it.<br /> <br /> Ryzala.<br /> <br /> Why Ryzala? Well canonically, she is supposed to the most powerful god after the Incarnae but as the goddess of bureaucracy I imagine that a lot of this power is rooted in a corrupt and inefficient infrastructure - she cannot really depend on the Celestial Lions, the Censors, the Aerial Legion and certainly not the Sidereals.<br /> <br /> I also envision her as one of those kinds of tyrants who believes she is completely indispensable, the status quo is imperfect but drastic change (such as her being demoted) would only bring the whole system crashing down. It is easy to place her in a situation where rules and regulations have failed, she needs muscle but none of the individuals who answer to her on paper can be trusted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","user":"Bastet","date":". 03-21-2015, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T22:44:16-07:00","id":453858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=404655#post404655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno how on-topic this is, but I had an idea for an Exigent. Their patron was a God of Treasure and Artiface, who had grown weaker with the decline of Creation's economy. So the God wanted a champion to bring the treasures of the First Age back to the fore, which might rekindle his Essence in ways that would even offset the Law of Diminishment somewhat. (Note: In a 'net gain' sense. The God would still be much weaker than if he had not granted the Exigence AND Creation started mass archeological digs, but was weak due to so much of the past being lost that he engaged in a desperate gamble)</div> </div> </div> </div>His name is Agralzo, God of Discovery (as in, scientific creation). He was created by Autochthon to basically be the God of Magitech, and was such a strong ally of the Twilights as the Director of the Bureau of Humanity that he was killed by Sidereals during the Usurpation. By the time he reformed, the fall in creativity and invention took away much of his power. Sentenced on trumped up charges to thousands of years of imprisonment, he's been in a Cage of Eternal Torment beneath the B. of Heaven's offices ever since. He would definitely want to work with new Exalted to gain his freedom, rediscover the past and to create new wonders, and would certainly desire access to the Exigence to create some for those purposes. He can be found on pg 57 of CoCD: Yu-Shan.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The resulting Exigent would be a metaphorical god among Scavenger Lords. 99% non-combat charms, for things like appraisal, mapping, and dungeon diving. Any combat skill would come from an affinity for artifact weapons, including the ability to unlock an artifact's Evocations. I don't know how viable or balanced that would be in Ex3, but I just love the idea. </div> </div> </div>Sounds awesome! Of course, he'll have to defeat MY Exigent, Chosen of Madame Marthesine of the Lost, who's mandate is to make sure that many things, places and lore of the past are/remain lost to the current Age...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T23:05:32-07:00","id":453876,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know if there is a god of Oasis or places of succor in otherwise inhospitable environments? I need a not-evil god that isn't the Endless Desert for... reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T23:18:21-07:00","id":453895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=453876#post453876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know if there is a god of Oasis or places of succor in otherwise inhospitable environments? I need a not-evil god that isn't the Endless Desert for... reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Master of Jade mention the Guild has made deal with various gods of oasis, I'm not sure if they have a big boss God of Oasis though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T23:28:15-07:00","id":453902,"title":"","content":"Huh, the one of the books I don't have. Rats. Thanks, though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T23:42:01-07:00","id":453914,"title":"","content":"IIRC, the Lotus Pool Court is a spirit court of Water Elementals who maintain oasises (?) in the deserts of Creation. Can Elementals have Exigents? There's probably an Oasis God in the Southern section of the Bureau of Seasons, if not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T00:05:28-07:00","id":453927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=453914#post453914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Elementals have Exigents? There's probably an Oasis God in the Southern section of the Bureau of Seasons, if not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, only gods can have Exigents, but there is always black market Exaltation.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T12:17:43-07:00","id":454707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=453858#post453858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His name is Agralzo, God of Discovery (as in, scientific creation). He was created by Autochthon to basically be the God of Magitech, and was such a strong ally of the Twilights as the Director of the Bureau of Humanity that he was killed by Sidereals during the Usurpation. By the time he reformed, the fall in creativity and invention took away much of his power. Sentenced on trumped up charges to thousands of years of imprisonment, he's been in a Cage of Eternal Torment beneath the B. of Heaven's offices ever since. He would definitely want to work with new Exalted to gain his freedom, rediscover the past and to create new wonders, and would certainly desire access to the Exigence to create some for those purposes. He can be found on pg 57 of CoCD: Yu-Shan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew the Bronze Faction were willing to do questionable things for their idea of the greater good, but just torturing somebody endlessly for thousands of years, just because he's inconvenient, even though they've already eliminated him as a threat? WTF.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T16:50:52-07:00","id":854735,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity how would you go about separating a MM exigent (like say Moonsilver) from a PAC using Sidereal or an Alchemical? Also what would be a good motivation for an MM god?<br /> Note:Not sure about the etiquette on bringing up older threads but I hope it is not an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T18:49:18-07:00","id":854791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=854735#post854735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity how would you go about separating a MM exigent (like say Moonsilver) from a PAC using Sidereal or an Alchemical? Also what would be a good motivation for an MM god?<br /> Note:Not sure about the etiquette on bringing up older threads but I hope it is not an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, for your first question, I'd say first focus on the core principles of the MM, and then expand upon them. Let us take Soulsteel as an example. In 2e, at least, it steals motes from the opponent and is shaped from oft-unwilling ghosts. We can see that Soulsteel is ultimately <i>vampiric</i>;it's all about taking something vital from another and using it to strengthen yourself. You can also think of ways in which the MM's themes differ from the presentation of the Caste or Exalt. Adamant, for example, is associated with Crystal*, the mind of Autochthon, and thus might focus on charms that give you a enhanced intellect rather than the stealthy assassination and infiltration favored by the operatives.<br /> <br /> As for your second, while each spirit is a unique individual with their own quirks and foibles, one thing to focus on is the propagation of their domain, which improves their own power and status. Thus, they want people to think about or need their particular MM. This means the protection and creation of Artifacts of the appropriate type as well as patronage of heroes who use this type of Artifact. They are likely to favor the Exalt type who naturally attunes to their MM, meaning that Jade might want to work to maintain the Realm(so Jade remains the One True Material in the eyes of the average Creationborn), while Orichalcum will fight tooth and nail to protect the newly returned Solars. <br /> <br /> Hope that helps!<br /> <br /> *Come to think of it, looking towards the Autochthonian element the MM is associated with seems to be a good way to gain additional thematic potential in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T19:00:23-07:00","id":854797,"title":"","content":"When creating an Exigent, always start with the specific god that created the Exigent. That's where your framework and flavor come from.<br /> <br /> Assuming that there is an actual god of soulsteel, you'll get a different Exigent if that god is the cadaverous Smith of the Frozen Forge than if that god is the thousand-fanged Prince of the Thirsty Blade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T19:54:09-07:00","id":854834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=854797#post854797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When creating an Exigent, always start with the specific god that created the Exigent. That's where your framework and flavor come from.<br /> <br /> Assuming that there is an actual god of soulsteel, you'll get a different Exigent if that god is the cadaverous Smith of the Frozen Forge than if that god is the thousand-fanged Prince of the Thirsty Blade.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an interesting angle although I kind of want to avoid dealing with soulsteel until a better picture of Yu Shan is presented since I have no idea where the loyalties of a Soulsteel god would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T19:56:53-07:00","id":854836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=854791#post854791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, for your first question, I'd say first focus on the core principles of the MM, and then expand upon them. Let us take Soulsteel as an example. In 2e, at least, it steals motes from the opponent and is shaped from oft-unwilling ghosts. We can see that Soulsteel is ultimately <i>vampiric</i>;it's all about taking something vital from another and using it to strengthen yourself. You can also think of ways in which the MM's themes differ from the presentation of the Caste or Exalt. Adamant, for example, is associated with Crystal*, the mind of Autochthon, and thus might focus on charms that give you a enhanced intellect rather than the stealthy assassination and infiltration favored by the operatives.<br /> <br /> As for your second, while each spirit is a unique individual with their own quirks and foibles, one thing to focus on is the propagation of their domain, which improves their own power and status. Thus, they want people to think about or need their particular MM. This means the protection and creation of Artifacts of the appropriate type as well as patronage of heroes who use this type of Artifact. They are likely to favor the Exalt type who naturally attunes to their MM, meaning that Jade might want to work to maintain the Realm(so Jade remains the One True Material in the eyes of the average Creationborn), while Orichalcum will fight tooth and nail to protect the newly returned Solars.*<br /> <br /> Hope that helps!<br /> <br /> *Come to think of it, looking towards the Autochthonian element the MM is associated with seems to be a good way to gain additional thematic potential in general.*</div> </div> </div> </div>That is very helpful, I am pretty curious as to where you would put the Starmetal god on this scale seeing as Starmetal is made by essentially damaging an important part of Astrology, something the Sidereals need and would probably be unhappy with any attempt to increase the production of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T16:12:44-07:00","id":878210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=452011#post452011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was saving this until my players found out about it.<br /> <br /> Ryzala.<br /> <br /> Why Ryzala? Well canonically, she is supposed to the most powerful god after the Incarnae but as the goddess of bureaucracy I imagine that a lot of this power is rooted in a corrupt and inefficient infrastructure - she cannot really depend on the Celestial Lions, the Censors, the Aerial Legion and certainly not the Sidereals.<br /> <br /> I also envision her as one of those kinds of tyrants who believes she is completely indispensable, the status quo is imperfect but drastic change (such as her being demoted) would only bring the whole system crashing down. It is easy to place her in a situation where rules and regulations have failed, she needs muscle but none of the individuals who answer to her on paper can be trusted.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This just gave me an idea. Forgive me if it has already been mentioned.<br /> <br /> The Arbiter, Exigent of a Celestial Censor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=854797#post854797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When creating an Exigent, always start with the specific god that created the Exigent. That's where your framework and flavor come from.<br /> <br /> Assuming that there is an actual god of soulsteel, you'll get a different Exigent if that god is the cadaverous Smith of the Frozen Forge than if that god is the thousand-fanged Prince of the Thirsty Blade.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very good point. What do you think an Exigent of Lytek would be like? Mild mannered Exigent, politico social butterfly with Influence among the Exalted Host?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2104-tenkage","name":"Tenkage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T17:09:31-07:00","id":878250,"title":"","content":"Although I think you're asking Eric, for Lytek, I think an Exigent would be.... very externally focused. He would craft, and he repairs and he understands. Both spiritually on souls and essences - human and animal and other - and also literally towards objects and physical things. He is attracted to and deals best with the traits (mental, emotional, physically) that make people strong and are spark to something greater. He can shame you, and inspire you, and influence you by showing the part of yourself that is worthy of Exaltation and how you are failing to achieve that.<br /> <br /> His internal power is probably almost totally focused on maintaining his ability to act externally, rather than to build up his inner strength, and being very resilient in the face of that which would turn him aside from his purpose, if that makes any sense. I don't see that Exigent as having a lot of power in a fight, because I don't see Lytek as offering a lot of power that's focused on stripping down and defeats or that would lend strength to his Exigent's sword arm (buffing armour and weapons to be more than they are works though, I think).<br /> <br /> I might be reaching, but I think his themes could lend themselves to an Exalt who was like a version of John the Baptist that fits Exalted's 'verse's cosmology and rules? As a sort of messianic figure who purifies and teaches others, and is a herald and prophet to power, and is so to such a degree that he's a significant person in himself. Maybe a calm and serene and mild mannered figure, or a firebrand driven by the inner purpose of the idea of Exaltation itself.<br /> <br /> (You could have his magic either literal dealing with other Exalted (the way the architect of Wu Jian in the core is very specifically a person inspired by a sitting dealing concretely with cities), or you could go the route where Exaltation is more of a motif and symbol (the way fields are to Janest? not just things she deals with, but with the harvest as a motif through all her abilities). Exigents seem to be able to take either.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T22:52:02-07:00","id":878501,"title":"","content":"I was responding to his quote but the idea of the Exigent is, of course, open to all for input.<br /> <br /> Looking at Lytek first is a good indicator of what to expect:<br /> <br /> Lytek as the God of Exaltation, specifically of Celestial Exalts, has questionable powers related to Exaltation. Especially given the new edition but hey, homebrew the blank spaces right?<br /> We do know he is a skilled bureaucrat, he has a untold knowledge of individual Exalts, their capabilities, as well as an awareness of the Great Curse.<br /> He can arguably teach any Charm to an Exalt type though he can not use any of those Exalted Charms he knows. He can also speed up Essence Training times in some versions.<br /> Looking at his domain also opens certain stories. Exaltation is about potentiality, heroism, and the power of the gods. Aspects of his domain he should be able to influence or affect: detecting Exalted, possibly even type, reading previous incarnations, pruning/keeping memories of previous Exalts, connecting an Exalt to his Past Life, etc...<br /> <br /> <br /> But I also agree that your idea is the a great vision of the Exigent of Lytek. As Exigents go, I would think about him being able to LEARN any Charm, but can only act as a tutor to valid users and he himself cannot use them. Same with spells.<br /> <br /> Thematically, I would focus on the following areas: Teaching/Tutoring/Mentoring/Coaching, Craftmanship, Inspiring/Uplifting/Empower, and Bureaucracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2104-tenkage","name":"Tenkage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T05:01:04-07:00","id":905552,"title":"","content":"A thought I had on what might drive a black market Exigence.<br /> <br /> \u200bMany weak gods are probably satisfied, or at least resigned, to being too far behind the curve to ever make so much as a decent entry in the game of divine politics. Your own Exalt would help, but the Unconquered Sun would never answer such a petition.<br /> <br /> Such a god is probably also too weak to make much of a bid in the necessary black markets, but a consortium of many might be able to pool assets and contacts sufficiently.<br /> <br /> They tell themselves that they'll find a way to share custody of it, and may even believe such, but one way or another they'll eventually start eliminating each other until only one remains.<br /> <br /> The resulting Exalt is probably only the Chosen of that god, but the violent and treacherous build up might give a certain edge to their powers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T05:26:07-07:00","id":905556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tenkage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=878210#post878210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Arbiter, Exigent of a Celestial Censor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Canonically, it would require a Censor who was a god rather than a Lesser Elemental Dragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T07:02:20-07:00","id":905596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=905552#post905552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-snip-</div> </div> </div> </div>An excellent idea! Consider it stolen at knifepoint!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T07:38:50-07:00","id":905626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=905552#post905552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thought I had on what might drive a black market Exigence.<br /> <br /> \u200bMany weak gods are probably satisfied, or at least resigned, to being too far behind the curve to ever make so much as a decent entry in the game of divine politics. Your own Exalt would help, but the Unconquered Sun would never answer such a petition.<br /> <br /> Such a god is probably also too weak to make much of a bid in the necessary black markets, but a consortium of many might be able to pool assets and contacts sufficiently.<br /> <br /> They tell themselves that they'll find a way to share custody of it, and may even believe such, but one way or another they'll eventually start eliminating each other until only one remains.<br /> <br /> The resulting Exalt is probably only the Chosen of that god, but the violent and treacherous build up might give a certain edge to their powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very cool idea!<br /> <br /> Though excitement about Exigents is making me more and more bummed we don't even have Dragonblooded yet, as it's seeming likely it'll be this time next year before we do get Exigents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T07:46:23-07:00","id":905632,"title":"","content":"I will say that one thing that complicates the issue of gods being new to something is the question of how often new gods come up.<br /> <br /> \u200bI myself have lower interest in the idea that the birth of new gods is anything other than a freak occurrence, mostly an oddity that comes from two or more gods having a dalliance or the occasional act of nature. I prefer the idea that most gods have been around since the beginning, or at least the beginning of their domains (which still amounts to most of them being unaccountably old). Maybe with a kind of generational thing; first the Incarnae, followed an indeterminate time after by various other key gods, then some time after that by the vast multiplicity that inhabits Heaven (the Blessed Isle, back then) and Earth, perhaps with a follow up around the Primordial War or at the start of the First Age (even then, I would assume that a lot of new domains for ascendant humanity are simply assigned to existing gods). Just the kind of thing that leaves the god you're likely to meet, even in Yu-Shan, uncertain about the origins of the world, or at least their kind.<br /> <br /> But how to reconcile this with something new?<br /> <br /> I would be inclined to two ideas:<br /> <br /> Gods who are killed without special Charms are eventually reborn. While this does generally take the form of the same character coming back, I'm drawn to the idea that some things could be lost in a manner that entails starting over somewhat; the same personality, but some of the memories become fuzzy. With or without that, it's probably mostly a case for how the interim period sends them back to square one, so one can have it that the course of spirit rivalries creates a reasonably high turnover that frequently generates gods who may as well be new.<br /> <br /> The other side is the picture of a god who was provincial and repetitive without issue until some circumstance or inexplicable motion within themselves shakes them out of their reverie, and they come out to society, so to speak. You have a dog of unbroken earth that never cared for anything but patrolling its particular patch of wilderness on the edge of civilisation, until some encounter or observation or revelation shakes their routine a bit, and they enter spirit society.<br /> <br /> I can imagine that part of what made the spirit courts in the Second Age so distinct was this happening to a lot of gods as a result of the Usurpation; they started to see the wider world, and wanted, and methods to sate want became a commodity in short supply.<br /> <br /> This all largely being a concern for Terrestrial gods; I would say that the Celestial Court is a good deal more rigid, at the same time as even the lowlier gods are more urbane. Still, I could imagine them having their own standards for new entry to society; the menial gods finding themselves promoted into the ever-expanding staff or court of a Celestial functionary, or some bureaucratic shuffling getting one assigned a newly designated domain or office, if not the standby of &quot;there are innumerable menial offices, some of which might occasionally gain a measure of significance&quot;, like what the Compass book did with that god of mergers.<br /> <br /> This is probably largely tangential to the topic of the thread, but it's a dilemma I've considered while reflecting on the idea of gods as disadvantaged newcomers as a motivation for illicit pursuit of Exalted when they're immortal and eternal, so I wanted to play it out. Besides, I would say that developing the Exigence can entail some consideration for the social context and motivations of gods, so it's not all wasted.<br /> <br /> Why, the scenario that makes a god proverbially enter society could even be a thing that makes them want an Exalt, in the sense of &quot;something must be done&quot; rather than &quot;I'll never close the XP gap, there are no potions for new subscribers&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T14:45:05-07:00","id":905968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence?p=905552#post905552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thought I had on what might drive a black market Exigence.<br /> <br /> \u200bMany weak gods are probably satisfied, or at least resigned, to being too far behind the curve to ever make so much as a decent entry in the game of divine politics. Your own Exalt would help, but the Unconquered Sun would never answer such a petition.<br /> <br /> Such a god is probably also too weak to make much of a bid in the necessary black markets, but a consortium of many might be able to pool assets and contacts sufficiently.<br /> <br /> They tell themselves that they'll find a way to share custody of it, and may even believe such, but one way or another they'll eventually start eliminating each other until only one remains.<br /> <br /> The resulting Exalt is probably only the Chosen of that god, but the violent and treacherous build up might give a certain edge to their powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I actually just had a similar thought about weak gods pooling together to get an exigence before I stumbled on this thread, and asked John about it via tweet. He indicated that that was a fairly unlikely scenario. He didn't say it was flat out impossible though, FWIW. I'm thinking to the extent it happens, it is likely as you said, via the black market, as opposed to officially granted by the UCS. At least, that's how I plan to handle it in my own campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,